WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Multiomic analysis shows regular exercise produces a distinct immune signature across RNA, epigenetics, metabolites, and lipids. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 188. A multi-omic blood assessment examined single-cell RNA, epigenetics, metabolites, lipids, and cells. The study compared people with regular exercise habits against those with sedentary lifestyles. Researchers identified a clear signature unique to the

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.780
exercise group. The work was published in science advances. The findings detail how physical

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:42.040
activity shapes multiple layers of immune function at once. This layered approach reveals coordinated

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:48.600
changes in immune parameters. Now shifting to imaging. Researchers applied AI to standard

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.700
heart echocardiograms to assess kidney structure and function. The approach uses existing cardiac

00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:01.540
images without additional scans. The study was published in Cell-Med. It demonstrates how routine

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:07.920
cardiac imaging can yield opportunistic kidney insights. The method expands diagnostic reach from

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.680
a single test. No new imaging equipment is required for the analysis. On a different note,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:19.980
a new study examined oligodendrocytes in health and disease states. The work shows these cells

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.700
cells' influence processes outside their traditional myelination function.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.540
Results appear in cell.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:30.160
The research broadens understanding of glial contributions to brain maintenance.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.000
It highlights previously underappreciated cellular activities.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:38.700
The findings shift focus from myelon alone to additional glial roles.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:45.700
Next up, analysis of nearly 500,000 UK biobank participants linked chronic inflammation

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.660
to poorer heart muscle and function.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:53.540
stress ranked among the strongest contributing factors. The study tracked long-term outcomes

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:58.860
across the population. Results were published in the European Journal of Preventive Cardiology.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.980
The data quantify how sustained inflammatory signals affect cardiac performance.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.600
The cohort size allows detection of subtle associations over time. Moving on,

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:15.300
passing brewed coffee through a paper filter captures and removes diterpenes. The method

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.160
prevents these compounds from reaching the final beverage. Observations come from nutrition

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.160
science tracking. The approach offers a simple, post-broost step for those monitoring

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:31.260
dyterpene intake. The filter acts after the brewing process is complete, shifting focus.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.360
A scoping review examined pre-clinical evidence for creatine in dementia models.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:42.020
Results across studies were consistently encouraging. Human evidence in older adults

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:47.640
remains small and heterogeneous. No randomizes trials in people living with dementia have been

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:53.300
completed yet. The review appears in recent literature summaries. The gap highlights the

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:59.860
need for controlled human studies. On another topic, research scientist Ashish Rajarkar examined

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:05.480
soybean plants with roots that grow straight down rather than spreading sideways. The modified

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:11.320
root architecture aims to improve performance under climate extremes. The plants may also store

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:16.400
more carbon in soil, work as underway at institution studying crop adaptation.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.920
The approach targets both yield stability and environmental benefits.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:25.840
Straight downward growth differs from typical lateral spread in standard varieties.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:27.900
Now to archaeology.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.460
Archaeologists uncovered a skeleton of a woman who lived in China about 700 years ago.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.740
The remains show signs consistent with historical accounts of nose cutting as punishment.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:44.500
No prior skeletal evidence had confirmed the practice, despite repeated mentions and texts.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.300
The Find offers the first potential physical record of this specific penalty.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:53.060
The skeleton dates to the medieval period in Chinese history.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:54.640
Changing direction.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.200
Three student theses from Elsebeth Schroeder's group at the Division of Quantum Device Physics

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.280
were published in scientific journals within three months.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:09.720
The papers explore how amino acids and a bone mineral influence magnesium implant degradation rates.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:13.780
The work addresses challenges in biodegradable medical materials.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.820
Publication of bachelor's thesis in journals remains uncommon.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.460
The findings focus on controlling breakdown speed in implant applications.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:29.160
Next, vaccines protected 80 to 100% of mice against lethal pneumonic plague.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:35.420
Protection held in mice engineered to lack interferon gamma, a signal previously considered

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.660
essential for survival.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.720
The study used multiple vaccine formulations.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.820
Results were reported in recent research summaries.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.300
The outcome challenges prior assumptions about required immune signals.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:53.060
On a genetics note, researchers performed transcriptome-based classification in mice

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.800
carrying autism spectrum disorder risk mutations.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:59.660
The approach grouped animals according to gene expression patterns.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.920
The study was published in Science.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.820
It provides a framework for categorizing molecular responses in genetic models.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.360
The classification relies on patterns observed across the transcriptome.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:12.880
Shifting topics.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:19.120
A 17-year seismic study documented reactivation of previously quiet faults beneath Mount

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:19.580
Mantap.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.920
The tests caused 1,399 local earthquakes.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:28.680
Activity continued to increase for years after the final test in 2017.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:33.460
The findings link underground nuclear activity to long-term fault behavior.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.520
The study covered an extended monitoring period.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.540
Now to social research.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:46.700
Researchers at the University of Amsterdam analyzed nearly 100,000 everyday conflicts on the Reddit page, MI The Asshole.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:52.160
People with power were singled out more quickly as culprits when responsibility was unclear.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.300
The study suggests observers assume powerful individuals can evade consequences.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.500
Results appear in the Journal of Personality and Social Psychology.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:05.860
The large sample allows statistical examination of everyday judgments.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.660
Changing subjects.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:11.980
The European Union has set a climate neutrality target for 2050.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:18.460
Researchers examine pathways across economic sectors that achieve substantial greenhouse gas reductions.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:24.340
The analysis indicates industrial capacity can be maintained alongside emission cuts.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:31.120
The work addresses feasibility of the 2050 goal. Multiple sectors were included in the pathway modeling.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:40.440
Finally, physicists at UC Santa Barbara extended the search for evidence of microscopic black holes produced at the large Hadron Collider.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.340
The method represents a new approach to looking for new particles.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:50.280
The formation of these objects has been proposed as one way to resolve anomalies in space-time

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:50.980
understanding.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.900
The study was reported by Fizz.org.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:57.520
The extension builds on prior collider data analysis.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:03.040
Something most people get wrong is the idea that mitochondria simply produce energy on

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.120
demand, like a steady power plant.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:11.400
In reality, they constantly decide whether to prioritize ATP generation or to support

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.660
cell growth and repair.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:18.960
Right now, inside your muscle cells, mitochondria are balancing these demands by shifting proteins

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.760
and substrates between pathways.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:27.380
A single cell can contain hundreds of mitochondria, each adjusting output based on nutrient availability

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:31.280
and signaling molecules such as mTOR and AMPK.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:37.000
One memorable number is that mitochondria can change their membrane potential by more

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.580
than 50 millivolts within minutes when nutrient conditions shift.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:46.900
The practical takeaway is that consistent movement and adequate protein intake give mitochondria

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:51.980
clearer signals about when to favor energy production versus when to support growth,

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:55.480
which may influence recovery and long-term cellular health.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:08:01.980
Before we go, keep an eye on further analysis of the multi-omic exercise data as additional

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.300
age groups are examined.

